cff-version: 1.2.0
message: >-
  If you use this software, please cite it as below, together with the
  references listed in this file (Silva 2003, for the original transit model,
  and Duque Estrada, Pinho & Valio 2025, for the Python implementation).
  For works in Portuguese or published in Brazil, please also cite
  Duque Estrada, Pinho & Valio 2026 (Revista Brasileira de Ensino de Fisica).
title: "ECLIPSE model: stellar activity and coronal mass ejections in planetary transit light curves"
type: software
authors:
  - given-names: Beatriz
    family-names: Duque Estrada
    affiliation: "CRAAM, Universidade Presbiteriana Mackenzie"
  - given-names: Felipe
    family-names: Pinho
    affiliation: "CRAAM, Universidade Presbiteriana Mackenzie"
  - given-names: Adriana
    family-names: Valio
    affiliation: "CRAAM, Universidade Presbiteriana Mackenzie"
repository-code: "https://github.com/Transit-Model-CRAAM/eclipse-model-star-activity"
license: GPL-3.0-or-later
abstract: >-
  Extension of the ECLIPSE planetary transit model (Python/C) to simulate stellar activity, including starspots, faculae and signatures compatible with coronal mass ejections, in planetary transit light curves, with MCMC fitting.
keywords:
  - exoplanets
  - planetary transits
  - starspots
  - stellar activity
  - coronal mass ejections
  - light curves
  - MCMC
